#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# string_position

#% text
# `string_position(s, p)` gives the positions `[start, end]` (1-based, inclusive) of the matches of the string pattern `p` in `s`; matches may overlap unless `overlaps: false`. `string_position(s, p, n)` gives at most `n`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
string_position("abxxabxxab", "ab")
#% output
#= [[1, 2], [5, 6], [9, 10]]

#% cell
string_position("aaaa", "aa")
#% output
#= [[1, 2], [2, 3], [3, 4]]

#% cell
string_position("aaaa", "aa", overlaps: false)
#% output
#= [[1, 2], [3, 4]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `string_cases`, `string_count`
